{"surface": "event", "title": "Microsoft's Azure growth falls below 48% in its January 27 report", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">Microsoft&#x27;s Azure growth falls below 48% in its January 27 report</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>The decision on Jan 27, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Microsoft fiscal Q2 2027 earnings release</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>At its fiscal second-quarter report, projected for January 27, 2027, Microsoft reports constant-currency growth in Azure and other cloud services below 48% for the December quarter: the acceleration from 48% in the September quarter stalls or reverses.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:74\" data-note=\"note:74\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Azure beat its own guidance by three to four points last quarter (48% against 44%-45%), and analysts look for 49%-50%. A print under 48% needs that pattern to break. What could break it: capacity (&#x27;capacity constraints prevented Azure from growing even faster&#x27;), this month&#x27;s outages, and capital spending that already came in below expectations. I put it a little above one in five.\"><p>Azure beat its own guidance by three to four points last quarter (48% against 44%-45%), and analysts look for 49%-50%. A print under 48% needs that pattern to break. What could break it: capacity (&#x27;capacity constraints prevented Azure from growing even faster&#x27;), this month&#x27;s outages, and capital spending that already came in below expectations. I put it a little above one in five.</p></div></div><h4 class=\"ev-k\">Evidence</h4><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:181\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:181:faf2325460a2\">Slowinski highlighted 48% constant-currency Azure growth in the fiscal first quarter, above management’s 44%-45% guidance, while Microsoft 365 Commercial Cloud grew 18%.</a></blockquote><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:181:3f6fe76d3cd0\">He expects Azure growth to accelerate further to 49%-50% in the fiscal second quarter and Microsoft 365 Commercial Cloud growth to reach 19%.</a></blockquote><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:181:cdc16a847c5f\">Munster also said capacity constraints prevented Azure from growing even faster, reinforcing Microsoft’s need for additional infrastructure investment.</a></blockquote></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"5\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:26\"><span class=\"n v\">22.0%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:26\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If Yes\"><span class=\"lab\">If Yes</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:26:yes\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$2,390</span></a></span><span class=\"cap\"><span class=\"n loss\">−0.48%</span> of portfolio</span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If No\"><span class=\"lab\">If No</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:26:no\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$674</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Full impact\"><span class=\"lab\">Full impact</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:swing:prop:26\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$3,064</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Volatility\"><span class=\"lab\">Volatility</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:volatility:prop:26\"><span class=\"n v\">±$1,469</span></a></span></div></div><nav class=\"tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button